  "foaf:name": "A Bottle of Science to the Ocean",
  "sdo:name": "A Bottle of Science to the Ocean",
  "sdo:description": "A Bottle of Science to the Ocean is an outreach initiative designed to bridge science and society by translating oceanographic knowledge into culturally resonant, engaging micropublications. Led by the Oceanographic and Antarctic Institute of the Ecuadorian Navy (INOCAR) with the support of the Permanent Commission for the South Pacific (CPPS), the project aims to amplify public understanding of the ocean through narratives, visuals, and voices rooted in local and traditional knowledge systems. It combines scientific communication, community engagement, and educational innovation in line with the Ocean Decade’s ocean literacy vision and cultural heritage priorities. Focused on Ecuador’s maritime jurisdiction, including the Galapagos Islands and Ecuador’s scientific expeditions to the Antarctic, the initiative is designed to be mobile-accessible and low-cost, targeting coastal populations and aiming to scale regionally across the Southeast Pacific.",
  "sdo:location": "Ecuador",
  "sdo:identifier": "47.9",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/a-bottle-of-science-to-the-ocean/",
